From: Onur Bingol <obingol@anaconda.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:53:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the broken-symlink case of TfAtomicOfstreamWrapper when
 symlinks are unavailable

TestErrorCases assumes TfSymlink always succeeds, but creating a symlink on
Windows requires SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege (administrator or Developer
Mode). The failing TF_AXIOM then aborts testTf with exit code 134, failing the
whole ctest entry. The same limitation is already handled elsewhere:
testenv/fileUtils.cpp stops testing symlinks after TfSymlink fails with EPERM,
and TestCommitSymlink in this file is guarded by ARCH_OS_WINDOWS with "Windows
has issues with the create symlink privilege". Only this block was missed
upstream. Keep the remaining TestErrorCases assertions running and skip just
the broken-symlink check when the symlink cannot be created.

Anaconda: fixes the TfAtomicOfstreamWrapper build-time test failure on Windows.

diff --git a/pxr/base/tf/testenv/atomicOfstreamWrapper.cpp b/pxr/base/tf/testenv/atomicOfstreamWrapper.cpp
--- a/pxr/base/tf/testenv/atomicOfstreamWrapper.cpp
+++ b/pxr/base/tf/testenv/atomicOfstreamWrapper.cpp
@@ -59,6 +59,9 @@
     }
 
     // Can't open files beneath a broken symlink
+    // Anaconda: creating a symlink requires a privilege that is not available
+    // on some Windows build machines, so skip this case there, as
+    // testenv/fileUtils.cpp does.
     {
         if (TfPathExists("broken_symlink")) {
             TF_AXIOM(ArchUnlinkFile("broken_symlink") == 0);
@@ -68,16 +71,19 @@
         }
 
         TF_AXIOM(TfMakeDir("dir-does-not-exist"));
-        TF_AXIOM(TfSymlink("dir-does-not-exist", "broken_symlink"));
+        const bool createdSymlink =
+            TfSymlink("dir-does-not-exist", "broken_symlink");
         TF_AXIOM(ArchRmDir("dir-does-not-exist") == 0);
 
-        {
+        if (createdSymlink) {
             std::string error;
             TfAtomicOfstreamWrapper wrapper("broken_symlink/foo.txt");
             const bool openedBrokenSymlink = wrapper.Open(&error);

             fprintf(stderr, "Expected error: %s\n", error.c_str());
             TF_AXIOM(!openedBrokenSymlink);
+        } else {
+            TF_WARN("Not testing atomic writes beneath a broken symlink");
         }
     }
 }
